# 06 — Reusable Code

Before writing new code, look for existing code you can reuse. Search `src/shared/` and nearby modules for helpers, types, and other elements that already do the job, and extend them instead of copying them.

When you write logic that other places also need, make it reusable. Skip reuse when it would put reliability, performance, user experience, or other goals at significant risk.
